# 9. PERFORMANCE INDICATORS AND KPI SCORING

Implement consistent, documented operational KPI definitions.

## Task Completion Rate

Completed eligible tasks divided by eligible assigned tasks within the selected reporting cohort.

## On-Time Completion Rate

Completed tasks finished on or before the applicable deadline divided by eligible completed tasks with valid deadlines.

## Current Overdue Tasks

Open tasks with deadlines earlier than the current Philippine business date or applicable deadline time.

## Pending Review

Tasks submitted for Manager approval but not yet approved or returned.

## Returned Submissions

Submission events returned for correction during the selected reporting period.

## Recognized Initiatives

Member Initiatives with final validated recognition.

## Daily Activity Compliance

Completed required activity submissions divided by applicable expected submissions.

## SLA Compliance

Eligible cases or requests completed within the defined SLA divided by eligible cases.

Implement configurable KPI targets and weights by personnel function.

Different operational positions must support different scoring criteria.

Do not score Regional Supervisors, Investigators, CCTV Operators, and Report Management Officers using one identical performance model.

Show:

- Calculation formula
- Numerator
- Denominator
- Reporting period
- Source records
- Last updated timestamp

Display **N/A** where insufficient data exists.

Do not treat zero assignments as poor performance.

Do not automatically generate employee disciplinary recommendations, employment decisions, or formal personnel ratings.

